<h1>Configuration</h1>
<p class="subtitle">Built-in defaults, one optional JSON file, then supported environment overrides.</p>

<h2 id="precedence">Resolution order</h2>
<ol>
  <li>The entrypoint selects the home directory from <code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_HOME</code>, defaulting to <code>~/.mcp-librarian</code>.</li>
  <li><code>loadConfig</code> starts with built-in defaults.</li>
  <li>It shallow-merges <code>&lt;home&gt;/config.json</code> when that file can be read and parsed.</li>
  <li>Supported environment variables override selected fields.</li>
</ol>
<p>A missing, unreadable, or malformed <code>config.json</code> is silently ignored. The home directory itself is fixed before the file is read, so a <code>home</code> key in that file does not relocate the installation.</p>

<h2 id="defaults">Built-in defaults</h2>
<div class="code-block">{
  <span class="kw">"logLevel"</span>: <span class="str">"info"</span>,
  <span class="kw">"rateLimit"</span>: <span class="val">200</span>,
  <span class="kw">"cacheSize"</span>: <span class="val">100</span>,
  <span class="kw">"cacheTtl"</span>: <span class="val">600000</span>,
  <span class="kw">"skillsRepo"</span>: <span class="str">"penumbraforge/mcp-librarian-skills"</span>,
  <span class="kw">"autoResearch"</span>: <span class="val">false</span>,
  <span class="kw">"qualityWeighting"</span>: <span class="val">true</span>,
  <span class="kw">"qualityWeight"</span>: <span class="val">0.4</span>,
  <span class="kw">"allowArbitraryPackUrls"</span>: <span class="val">false</span>
}</div>

<h2 id="config-file">config.json</h2>
<p>Example:</p>
<div class="code-block">{
  <span class="kw">"logLevel"</span>: <span class="str">"warning"</span>,
  <span class="kw">"rateLimit"</span>: <span class="val">100</span>,
  <span class="kw">"cacheSize"</span>: <span class="val">50</span>,
  <span class="kw">"cacheTtl"</span>: <span class="val">300000</span>,
  <span class="kw">"skillsRepo"</span>: <span class="str">"example/team-skills"</span>,
  <span class="kw">"autoResearch"</span>: <span class="val">false</span>,
  <span class="kw">"qualityWeighting"</span>: <span class="val">true</span>,
  <span class="kw">"qualityWeight"</span>: <span class="val">0.25</span>,
  <span class="kw">"allowArbitraryPackUrls"</span>: <span class="val">false</span>
}</div>

<p><code>qualityWeighting</code> and <code>allowArbitraryPackUrls</code> currently have no environment-variable equivalents. <code>allowArbitraryPackUrls</code> weakens the pack URL boundary; see <a href="/librarian/wiki/community-packs/">Community Packs</a>.</p>

<h2 id="environment">Environment variables</h2>
<table class="cmd-table"><thead><tr><th>Variable</th><th>Default</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_HOME</code></td><td><code>~/.mcp-librarian</code></td><td>Selects the base directory before config loading.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_LOG_LEVEL</code></td><td><code>info</code></td><td><code>debug</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>warning</code>, or <code>error</code>. Invalid values fall back to <code>info</code>. The valid name is <code>warning</code>, not <code>warn</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_RATE_LIMIT</code></td><td><code>200</code></td><td>Positive finite number. An invalid or zero environment value falls back to 200.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_CACHE_SIZE</code></td><td><code>100</code></td><td>Positive finite number of content-cache entries; invalid environment input falls back to 100.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_CACHE_TTL</code></td><td><code>600000</code></td><td>Positive finite cache lifetime in milliseconds; invalid environment input falls back to the default.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_SKILLS_REPO</code></td><td><code>penumbraforge/mcp-librarian-skills</code></td><td>Repository path used by pack browsing and named installs.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_AUTO_RESEARCH</code></td><td><code>false</code></td><td>Only <code>1</code> or case-insensitive <code>true</code> enables the conditional <code>find_and_load</code> network path.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_QUALITY_WEIGHT</code></td><td><code>0.4</code></td><td>Number from 0 through 1. Invalid environment input falls back to 0.4.</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code></td><td>unset</td><td>Read directly by the pack downloader and sent only to <code>raw.githubusercontent.com</code> or <code>api.github.com</code>.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<div class="warning-box"><strong>File values are not uniformly validated.</strong> <code>logLevel</code> from the file is validated, and the store clamps <code>qualityWeight</code>, but numeric file values such as <code>rateLimit</code>, <code>cacheSize</code>, and <code>cacheTtl</code> do not receive the same positive-number validation as environment overrides. For example, <code>rateLimit: 0</code> in the file can block all non-exempt requests; <code>MCP_LIBRARIAN_RATE_LIMIT=0</code> instead falls back to 200.</div>

<h2 id="layout">Actual on-disk layout</h2>
<div class="code-block"><span class="dim">~/.mcp-librarian/</span>
<span class="dim">  config.json</span>              <span class="cmt"># optional, user-created</span>
<span class="dim">  manifest.json</span>            <span class="cmt"># hashes, signatures, timestamps</span>
<span class="dim">  keys/</span>
<span class="dim">    private.pem</span>
<span class="dim">    public.pem</span>
<span class="dim">  skills/</span>
<span class="dim">    getting-started.md</span>     <span class="cmt"># flat files only</span>
<span class="dim">    api-design.md</span>
<span class="dim">  exports/</span>                <span class="cmt"># created on first export</span>
<span class="dim">    team-patterns/</span>
<span class="dim">      pack.json</span>
<span class="dim">      api-design.md</span></div>

<p>There is no persistent <code>index/</code>, <code>signatures/</code>, or <code>logs/</code> tree in the current implementation. The BM25 index, term statistics, and LRU content cache live in memory and are rebuilt from flat skill files at process start or after supported mutations.</p>
<p>The installer writes both PEM files with mode <code>0600</code>. <code>manifest.json</code> contains a top-level timestamp and per-skill hash, signature, and signing timestamp.</p>

<h2 id="logging">Logging</h2>
<p>Logs are MCP <code>notifications/message</code> messages sent over stdio. They are not appended to a file. Severity order is <code>debug</code>, <code>info</code>, <code>warning</code>, <code>error</code>.</p>
<p>The server emits a startup message and, after client initialization, a skill catalog at <code>info</code>. Clients decide whether and where those notifications appear. MCP's <code>logging/setLevel</code> changes the dispatcher's logger threshold at runtime; the entrypoint also owns a logger initialized from config, so not every emitter necessarily shares that later change.</p>

<h2 id="rate-limiting">Rate limiting</h2>
<p>The dispatcher keeps request timestamps in memory and applies a sliding 60-second window. <code>initialize</code>, <code>initialized</code>, and <code>ping</code> are exempt. This is a request-loop guard; it is not a per-domain web crawler limit or a persistent quota.</p>

<h2 id="client">Server entrypoint</h2>
<div class="code-block">{
  <span class="kw">"mcpServers"</span>: {
    <span class="kw">"mcp-librarian"</span>: {
      <span class="kw">"command"</span>: <span class="str">"node"</span>,
      <span class="kw">"args"</span>: [<span class="str">"/absolute/path/to/mcp-librarian/bin/mcp-librarian.js"</span>]
    }
  }
}</div>
<p>The runtime is stdio-only. The repository does not expose an HTTP server, daemon socket, <code>server.js</code>, or direct model-provider configuration.</p>
